On 2007-08-07, Henry J Cobb <hcobb@io.com> wrote:
> And while the polearm memory function is helpful, it also tracks 
> critters that I can't see at the moment.
>
> Bug?

The polearm memory function will also track creatures who move to places a
polearm cannot reach -- or to places your current skill level in polearm
cannot reach.  This might include around corners.

It can be assumed that the player sees the monster step around the corner,
and thus "remembers" where it is even though he cannot hit there.

It would be more of a bug if a monster, say, teleported out of the
player's vision, left the level via cursed teleport, or became
invisible; all of these should reset the polearm target, which AFAIK
they don't currently do.

